import json
D = []
def add(i, d, q, r, c=None):
    o = {"item_id": i, "decision": d, "quote": q, "reason": r}
    if c is not None: o["corrected"] = c
    D.append(o)
add("D041","Y","The investigation confirmed that JATCO Mexico was exclusive in utilizing the affected inhibitor switch manufactured at Valeo Thailand.","Both SUPPORTED with same quote; Y gives the required 'name' field with the name as the narrative writes it (Valeo Thailand); X lacks the name field.")
add("D042","CONTESTED","February 2026 - The supplier conducted an initial teardown and evaluation of the suspect control valve assembly. Initial findings indicated a lack of electrical contact between Terminal Block SW#2 within the inhibitor switch of the transmission control valve assembly.","The two versions describe different sentences of the same February 2026 entry: the teardown (correctly INVESTIGATION_START) and the inherited-date findings sentence (correctly OTHER, test result). Each is a valid event in its own right; the pairing cannot be resolved as one right/one wrong.")
add("D043","Y","Throughout this month the supplier collected and analyzed a total of five (5) failed parts returned from the field and three (3) failed parts returned from the plant.","Analysis of failed parts conducted to find the cause is INVESTIGATION_START.")
add("D044","X","JATCO determined that all verified failed components were manufactured from October 17, 2025 to October 18, 2025.","JATCO is the transmission supplier reporting a finding on the problem; rules list 'the supplier confirmed ...' as SUPPLIER_NOTICE. The Oct 17-18 dates bound a production window and are ignored.")
add("D045","X","A review of the sub-supplier’s manufacturing process for the inhibitor switch found that a locator pin may have broken on the production line on October 17, 2025.","This sentence starts a new paragraph after a blank line, so it is outside the March 2026 entry; it carries its own date (October 17, 2025) and is captured by D052. A March-inherited event is wrong.")
add("D046","Y","A broken locator pin in service at the riveting stage may contribute to misalignment and result in a terminal height variation within the inhibitor switch housing.","Description of a possible mechanism, no action or occurrence; not an event.")
add("D047","X","This condition may contribute to the electrical continuity concern.","Description/assumption with no action; not an event.")
add("D048","NEITHER","In response, part sorting and yard audits were initiated based on the affected date code.","Containment action is an event (OTHER), but it is in a new paragraph after a blank line, outside the March 2026 entry, with no date of its own: undated prose, date_inferred.",
    {"date_text":"","type":"OTHER","quote":"In response, part sorting and yard audits were initiated based on the affected date code.","inherited_date":False,"date_inferred":True})
add("D049","NEITHER","JATCO conducted traceability analysis to identify control valve assemblies containing suspect inhibitor switches (produced October 17–18, 2025) and link them to specific continuously variable transmissions (CVTs).","Event exists but is outside the March entry (after a blank line) and the Oct 17-18 dates only bound a production window, so it is undated prose (date_inferred). Traceability analysis to determine scope is INVESTIGATION_START.",
    {"date_text":"","type":"INVESTIGATION_START","quote":"JATCO conducted traceability analysis to identify control valve assemblies containing suspect inhibitor switches (produced October 17–18, 2025) and link them to specific continuously variable transmissions (CVTs).","inherited_date":False,"date_inferred":True})
add("D050","NEITHER","The supplier part audit and Smyrna plant vehicle audit identified 76 suspect parts (42 vehicles and 3 CVTs at Nissan North America Smyrna Plant, and 31 control valve assemblies at JATCO Mexico).","Audit result is an event (OTHER), but it sits in the paragraph after the blank line, outside the March 2026 entry, with no own date: undated prose, date_inferred.",
    {"date_text":"","type":"OTHER","quote":"The supplier part audit and Smyrna plant vehicle audit identified 76 suspect parts (42 vehicles and 3 CVTs at Nissan North America Smyrna Plant, and 31 control valve assemblies at JATCO Mexico).","inherited_date":False,"date_inferred":True})
add("D051","Y","Traceability data confirmed that the first vehicle built using a transmission made during the identified manufacturing window occurred on January 13, 2026.","January 13, 2026 only bounds the affected production window (first build date), so it is not an event date; the sentence's event inherits the April-May 2026 entry date (D053).")
add("D052","X","A review of the sub-supplier’s manufacturing process for the inhibitor switch found that a locator pin may have broken on the production line on October 17, 2025.","Sentence is outside any dated entry and has its own date October 17, 2025; finding of the review is an event (OTHER).")
add("D053","X","April 2026 through May 2026 - Nissan conducted a horizontal confirmation audit to determine the scope of potentially affected vehicles, including export markets and other vehicle lines.","The traceability finding is inside the April-May 2026 dated entry (no blank line before it); its own Jan 13 date is a production-window bound, so it inherits the entry date.")
add("D054","X","From April 2026 through May 2026, FCA US TSRC conducted an analysis of field records and customer assistance records to understand potential customer consequences.","Analysis aimed at customer consequences, not at cause or scope (the investigation was already opened April 16); OTHER under the rules.")
add("D055","Y","On June 10, 2026, FCA US TSRC organization recognized that a vehicle build issue existed on certain vehicles related to premium headlamp assemblies, potentially resulting in a noncompliance with FMVSS No. 108.","Filer becomes aware/recognizes a problem exists; FILER_AWARENESS covers later awareness. Not yet the decision (June 25).")
add("D056","Y","An investigation occurred and determined that the bolt may contact the fuel line.","An investigation conducted to find the cause is INVESTIGATION_START.")
add("D057","Y","2026-06-18 An analysis of all our ambulance models was conducted, and it was determined that only this model was affected.","Analysis conducted to determine scope is INVESTIGATION_START.")
add("D058","X","July 2nd, a search was completed for all vehicles equipped with the effected models of liftgates all four were matched to vehicles that were delivered to customers between 2024 and 2025.","Search conducted to determine scope of affected vehicles is INVESTIGATION_START.")
add("D059","X","Nissan initiated an investigation into this potential concern.","Narrative only names Nissan (the filer); it never names Nissan Shatai Kyusyu as supplier. Block name is not a name in narrative, so INSUFFICIENT with the block Name line; Y's quote does not name the supplier.")
add("D060","X","April 2026 through May 2026, Nissan initiated a horizontal evaluation to identify the scope of potentially affected vehicles.","Evaluation started to identify scope is INVESTIGATION_START.")
add("D061","X","Between November 2025 and April 2026, the investigation continued, and was focused on analysis of the wear process of the contact pin.","Range is one period as written (Y truncates to April 2026); investigation conducted on cause (wear process) fits INVESTIGATION_START.")
add("D062","Y","In April 2026, a detailed analysis involving field data, and statistical forecasting, was initiated.","An analysis was initiated: INVESTIGATION_START.")
add("D063","Y","May 12, 2026, through July 10, 2026, the investigation continued.","date_text should be the full range as written; investigation conducted is INVESTIGATION_START (X truncates the date).")
add("D064","Y","On July 28, 2026, OCC and the plant discovered that some vehicles may have been shipped.","Filer 'discovered' that affected vehicles reached the field; rules list 'discovered' as FILER_AWARENESS.")
json.dump(D, open("decisions.json","w"), indent=1, ensure_ascii=False)
